.TH "S3AR\-LIST" "1" "October 2026" "S3 Archiver" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
s3ar\-list \- list live S3 buckets and objects
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
s3ar\-list [\-v] [\-b] [\-o] [FIELDS] [\-\-delimiter STRING] s3://[BUCKET[/KEY]]...
s3ar\-list \-b [\-v] s3://
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]\f[CB]s3ar\-list\f[B]\f[R] lists live S3 buckets and objects selected by
one or more S3 URIs.
The URI \f[B]\f[CB]s3://\f[B]\f[R] selects all buckets and their objects.
A bucket URI selects that bucket and its objects; a key URI selects the exact
key and keys below KEY/.
Matches stop at path boundaries, and a trailing slash does not change the
selection.
See \f[B]\f[CB]s3ar(1)\f[B]\f[R] for selection examples.
.PP
Bucket and key names in operands are literal, not URL\-decoded.
Quote operands containing spaces or shell metacharacters.
Operands are processed in order; overlapping selections produce repeated output.
A key selection that matches neither an object nor descendants is an error.
Empty buckets are valid.
.PP
Listing results are written to standard output; diagnostics go to standard
error.
When bucket output is enabled, bucket names are printed before their selected
objects, including for key selections.
Names have the \f[B]\f[CB]s3://\f[B]\f[R] prefix and use the byte\-oriented URL
encoding described in \f[B]\f[CB]s3ar(1).\f[B]\f[R]
.PP
The URI is followed by requested fields in command\-line option order, without
field names or prefixes.
Repeated requests for the same field use its first position.
Object fields apply to object rows; bucket ACL applies to bucket rows.
.PP
Fields are separated by a space by default.
Records end with a newline.
Missing values produce empty fields, including at the end of a record.
Selected metadata values are printed as received, without added quoting or
encoding.
For parsing, use \f[B]\f[CB]\-\-delimiter\f[B]\f[R] to choose a separator that
does not occur in the values and preserve empty fields and trailing separators.
.PP
For example:
.IP
.EX
s3ar\-list \-o \-\-object\-meta source \-\-object\-size \-\-delimiter \[aq]|\[aq] s3://bucket/
s3://bucket/a|manual upload|123
s3://bucket/b||456
.EE
.SH OPTIONS
\f[B]\f[CB]\-b, \-\-buckets\f[B]\f[R]
.PP
Include bucket rows.
Without \f[B]\f[CB]\-o,\f[B]\f[R] list buckets only and require exactly one
operand, \f[B]\f[CB]s3://.\f[B]\f[R]
.PP
\f[B]\f[CB]\-o, \-\-objects\f[B]\f[R]
.PP
Include object rows.
Without \f[B]\f[CB]\-b,\f[B]\f[R] omit bucket rows; an empty bucket produces
empty successful output.
Combine as \f[B]\f[CB]\-bo\f[B]\f[R] for both row types.
If neither option is given, both row types are enabled.
.PP
\f[B]\f[CB]\-\-object\-size\f[B]\f[R]
.PP
Append object size in bytes.
.PP
\f[B]\f[CB]\-\-object\-mtime\f[B]\f[R]
.PP
Append object modification time in seconds since the Unix epoch.
.PP
\f[B]\f[CB]\-\-object\-etag\f[B]\f[R]
.PP
Append object ETag, or an empty field if unavailable.
Object field options require object output.
.PP
\f[B]\f[CB]\-\-object\-metadata\f[B]\f[R]
.PP
Append all user metadata as one compact JSON object with keys sorted by name.
An object with no metadata produces \f[B]\f[CB]{}.\f[B]\f[R] JSON strings use
standard JSON escaping; the JSON object is not percent\-encoded.
.PP
\f[B]\f[CB]\-\-object\-meta NAME\f[B]\f[R]
.PP
Append one user metadata value.
Repeat to select multiple fields.
Names are case\-insensitive and omit the \f[B]\f[CB]x\-amz\-meta\-\f[B]\f[R]
prefix.
Missing and empty values both produce an empty field.
Can be combined with \f[B]\f[CB]\-\-object\-metadata.\f[B]\f[R]
.PP
Both metadata options require object output and make an additional HEAD request
for each listed object.
Multiple metadata options share one HEAD request per object.
A failed HEAD request fails the listing.
.PP
\f[B]\f[CB]\-\-delimiter STRING\f[B]\f[R]
.PP
Separate fields with STRING instead of a space.
Supports \f[B]\f[CB]\[rs]t,\f[B]\f[R] \f[B]\f[CB]\[rs]n,\f[B]\f[R]
\f[B]\f[CB]\[rs]0,\f[B]\f[R] and \f[B]\f[CB]\[rs]\[rs]\f[B]\f[R] for tab,
newline, NUL, and backslash.
Other escapes and a trailing backslash are errors.
Quote the argument to preserve backslashes, for example
\f[B]\f[CB]\-\-delimiter \[aq]\[rs]t\[aq].\f[B]\f[R] An empty string joins
fields without a separator.
If repeated, the last value is used.
Record endings remain newlines.
.PP
\f[B]\f[CB]\-\-bucket\-acl\f[B]\f[R]
.PP
Fetch and append bucket ACL information.
Requires bucket output.
.PP
\f[B]\f[CB]\-v, \-\-verbose\f[B]\f[R]
.PP
Increase diagnostic verbosity: one occurrence enables info diagnostics, two
enable debug, and three enable HTTP trace.
Further occurrences have no effect.
.PP
\f[B]\f[CB]\-h, \-\-help\f[B]\f[R]
.PP
Display command usage on standard error and exit successfully.
.SH EXAMPLES
List all visible buckets:
.IP
.EX
s3ar\-list \-b s3://
.EE
.PP
List objects under a selection, adding modification time and size:
.IP
.EX
s3ar\-list \-o \-\-object\-mtime \-\-object\-size s3://photos/2026/
.EE
.PP
Select user metadata and size with a pipe separator:
.IP
.EX
s3ar\-list \-o \-\-object\-meta source \-\-object\-size \-\-delimiter \[aq]|\[aq] s3://photos/
.EE
.PP
For example, a missing metadata value produces an empty field:
.IP
.EX
s3://photos/a.jpg|manual upload|12345
s3://photos/b.jpg||456
.EE
.PP
List all user metadata as JSON, separating fields with a tab:
.IP
.EX
s3ar\-list \-o \-\-object\-metadata \-\-delimiter \[aq]\[rs]t\[aq] s3://photos/
.EE
.SH SIGNALS
\f[B]\f[CB]SIGUSR1\f[B]\f[R]
.PP
Increase diagnostic verbosity by one level, up to trace.
.PP
\f[B]\f[CB]SIGUSR2\f[B]\f[R]
.PP
Decrease diagnostic verbosity by one level, down to fatal.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
\f[B]\f[CB]S3AR_ENDPOINT,\f[B]\f[R] \f[B]\f[CB]S3AR_REGION,\f[B]\f[R]
\f[B]\f[CB]S3AR_URI_STYLE,\f[B]\f[R] \f[B]\f[CB]S3AR_ACCESS_KEY,\f[B]\f[R]
\f[B]\f[CB]S3AR_SECRET_KEY,\f[B]\f[R] and
\f[B]\f[CB]S3AR_SESSION_TOKEN\f[B]\f[R] configure the S3 connection in the same
way as for \f[B]\f[CB]s3ar(1).\f[B]\f[R]
.SH EXIT STATUS
\f[B]\f[CB]0\f[B]\f[R]
.PP
The listing or help completed successfully.
.PP
\f[B]\f[CB]1\f[B]\f[R]
.PP
S3 client initialization or standard\-output flush failed.
.PP
\f[B]\f[CB]2\f[B]\f[R]
.PP
Invalid usage, invalid configuration, allocation failure, or an S3 operation
failed.
.PP
When an S3 operation fails after a retry, the diagnostic includes the number of
attempts.
